X:1
T:Deffrwch! Benteulu (version 2)
T:Awake! Head of the Family
R:cân
S:https://amgueddfa.cymru/casgliadau/caneuongwerin/?id=18 (collected by D. Roy Saer)
N:Sung by Phillip Owen (born 1879), a farmer of 60 Non Street, St David's, Pembrokeshire; recorded 12.9.63 (St Fagans tape 610). A New Year quête (begging) rhyme: when he was about seven, children in the St David's area sang it at the doors on Christmas and New Year's mornings.
N:The last note is printed as a cross: its exact pitch was lost as the singer broke into laughter.
%%version Phillip Owen
